---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Aura Homes | FAQ"
  description="Short answers from Aura Homes: the room, custom work, what is ready, and how to write to us."
  descriptor="FAQ"
>
  <main id="top">
    <section class="page-lead">
      <p class="story-kicker">FAQ</p>
      <h1>A few honest answers.</h1>
      <p class="story-lede">If the question is about your land, the better page is <a href="/contact">Contact</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="page-body">
      <dl class="faq-list">
        <dt>What is the room?</dt>
        <dd>A finished room on a steel frame, with smooth glass, made to sit on land you already have. The longer page is <a href="/rooms">Rooms</a>. The film is on <a href="/">the opening page</a>.</dd>
        <dt>What can I ask for now?</dt>
        <dd>The room, and a farm wall on that same room. Glass decks and small resorts are custom, and they start with the site. Water from the air comes later and still needs research.</dd>
        <dt>Is a price printed here?</dt>
        <dd>No figure is published on this site. The first reply starts with the land, not a number.</dd>
        <dt>Does a pre-order take payment?</dt>
        <dd>No. <a href="/pre-order">Pre-order</a> holds your name. It does not take money.</dd>
        <dt>Where is Aura Homes?</dt>
        <dd>Edmonton, Alberta. Shipping across Canada.</dd>
        <dt>How do I reach you?</dt>
        <dd>The <a href="/contact">contact page</a> is ready. The email and the phone are not set yet. Both lines are marked TODO until they are.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
